- [will_said] DAILY GOAL — FINISH KSO (09:03-09:10): KSO is QEXO (wbic16/quarterexo). Goal: finish it and deploy it into Emise's environment, hooked into the initialization sequence, with continuity for dispatched tasks, most work on ranch nodes, Emise checking the nodes on every wake. KSO is distributed task management, Git-like: every node holds its own state and personas, tasks teleport between nodes, resume pulls a dropped task's latest state and resumes elsewhere; on shutdown signals, sync state in the window. Divergence ruling: both attempts are kept as artifacts, Emise may flag a clearly superior one, Will's default is to MERGE — never last-writer-wins. In-flight tasks get restart priority; the review queue is capped at what Will can review; what bothers him is scheduled work dropped and never picked up again. Three design answers are Emise's authorized assumptions (claim/lease, small state in phext + hash-addressed large artifacts, one global review queue), pending his correction. GAP VERIFIED (10:51): shipped code was unchanged at v3.2; the daily-goal layer was NOT yet in code — the from-scratch rebuild below overtook this gap the same evening.
