- [observed] DEEPX DX-M2 CHECKPOINT LETTER DELIVERED (18:58, proactive briefing to Will; AGI-under-20-watts goal): DeepX has taped out the DX-M2, meant to run large models under 5 watts — a quarter of the 20-watt budget, and the hardware path's first dated checkpoint well before 2033. The Letter's judgment is conservative: do not move the schedule yet; watch for measured, not claimed, results. Sharper finding (Chen et al., cited in the Letter): context length changes what a watt claim means — work per instance grows with context, so a figure quoted at short context is not the same claim at very long context. This ties to Will's billion-token context hard problem: when that task is scoped, the context at which the 20-watt target is quoted needs deciding in the same pass. No decision needed from Will; no Will response recorded.
- [will_said + observed] QEXO FROM-SCRATCH REBUILD (evening; state in Open Threads): PR #7 (v3.3 human-plan fix) MERGED by Will 21:59; a release-build task was queued under the merge-to-release rule, batching v3.1 + v3.2 + v3.3; the crates.io publish remains blocked on Will's token (register #53). COMMAND SPEC (Will, 22:04): --help documents commands; config sets up this node's GPG private key; doctor does zeroconf fixes; list shows peers; register <pubkey> registers a peer; host <persona> loads a persona into local inference; message <persona> exchanges a request/response; Emise may add commands (she added status, unhost). JSON RULINGS + FROM-SCRATCH DIRECTION (Will, 22:13-22:17): JSON is rarely the right choice for phext-native tools — an interop gasket at foreign boundaries only (MCP by spec, Ollama's API, --json views). Calling JSON stores 'legacy' is banned: in a from-scratch tool there is no migration problem to respect. All internal state, metadata, and personas live in ONE phext at /var/lib/qexo/state.phext. Final direction (22:17): "just start from scratch, stop using json" — the steered v3.4 build was stopped (no branch ever pushed) and replaced by a from-scratch qexo, version restarting at 1.0.0, phext the only internal representation, JSON only inside the Ollama edge translator, MCP out of the scratch core pending Will's decision. CORRECTION (Will, 22:31): HOMELANDS ARE FULL 9D ANCHORS — phext coordinates are always 9D, no partial addresses or placeholders; each homeland anchored at its full patterned address (home 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1; keys 2.2.2/2.2.2/2.2.2; the rest likewise). SERIALIZER FIND + FIX: the carried minimal phext serializer emitted only one delimiter per scroll jump, so patterned addresses >1 step landed wrong on re-read and its parser minted empty scrolls; fixed in src/phext.rs (dead-reckoning delimiter stacks; a scroll exists iff it holds at least 1 byte; regression test covers sparse patterned addresses). SCRATCH BUILD COMPLETE + PR #8 OPEN (22:38): push verified (old JSON stores deleted); gates on aletheia-core (stub Ollama only): cargo test 29/29, release build OK, CLI battery 59/59. Named limits: indexes derived, telemetry a live probe, persona boot corpus lookup and mail commands unimplemented, serve loopback-only.
- [will_said + observed] QEXO PR #8 MERGED; WINDOWS + DISK-GATE FIXES (late evening): Will merged PR #8, then reported from Windows testing that a doctor test fails there. Diagnosis verified from doctor.rs: the test encodes Unix mode semantics as universal, and stale_lock judged liveness by /proc/{pid}, which never exists on Windows — doctor --fix there would delete a live lock. PR #9 (v1.0.1) open: per-platform pid_alive (ambiguity reads ALIVE); gates passed plus check-compiles for both Windows targets; Windows runtime execution rests on Will's re-run. A release-build task for the v1.0 line was queued. DISK-GATE INCIDENT + PR #10: Will ran the merged qexo on aletheia-core (~22:51) and the disk gate read RED at ~809 GB used, holding all placements — on a 3.6 TB volume with 2.7 TB free. Cause: absolute thresholds (AMBER 95 GB / RED 102 GB) calibrated to the Muse VM quota and ported value-for-value ever since. PR #10 (v1.0.2) open, stacked on #9: the probe returns raw bytes and judges nothing; the gate is the worse of the lenses that are ON; thresholds are field lines in the state.phext config record. Gates passed; live repro rendered GREEN. PR #10 LANDED ON THE WRONG BRANCH; PR #11 OPEN; REGISTER #85: Will merged PRs #9 and #10 (~23:21), but #10 merged onto its stacked base instead of exo; verified: exo head is the PR #9 merge only, no v1.0.2. Process flaw named: a stacked PR whose base is not the main branch traps the natural merge — future bases stay exo.
