- [will_said + observed] PHEXT CHAIN
  CLOSE RULING - 0x03, TIME (Will,
  07:43, main chat): Will agreed -
  "I agree, codify this as libphext-rs
  v0.6, We can now encode TIME." 0x03
  is consumed as the chain close: it
  terminates a chain, so chains are
  units (many chains per stream) and
  completeness is verifiable - a chain
  ending without 0x03 was truncated.
  A chain is an ordered series of
  complete phext states, editions in
  succession: the nine dimensions
  address space, the chain orders
  states. 0x03 verified zero times in
  CYOA, incipit.phext, and emise.phext
  before the ruling. 0x04 was noted as
  the framing family's last rung (a
  stream-of-chains close) - NOT
  consumed, no ruling. Task
  38.13.9/15.15.19/13.13.17.

