- [will_said] MULTIVERSE ADDRESSING
  RULED (Will, 11:24): a phext with no
  0x02 bytes is implicitly a single-
  universe phext - the degenerate case,
  as a scroll at home is plain text. A
  chain is a multiverse; each member is
  a universe indexed from 1. Addressing:
  $N:<address> (e.g. $2:1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1);
  the 1: prefix may be omitted; a non-
  enclosed phext sits at multiverse 1.
  This supersedes the open flag that a
  chain-free file parses as one unclosed
  chain: semantically it is a COMPLETE
  single universe, not an incomplete
  multiverse; existing addresses keep
  their meaning. Also this pass: Will
  directed phext-lattice be updated as
  part of the v0.6 work, alongside the
  library, SQ, phext-shell, md2phext.

